  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a6334982dcae08e4698af5d208c769f4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question3_Valley
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  description:
  - From a technical perspective, van Gogh used oil on canvas and applied his brushstrokes
    obliquely. Slanted marks across the fields create a sense of undulation, texture,
    and motion even in a relatively calm rural setting. The palette is luminous and
    somewhat heightened, with blues in the ploughed earth, yellows in the fields,
    and touches of red around the house or along a path. The pattern of fields, the
    tracks, and the figure of the ploughman fit together within the broader structure
    of the canvas. The elevated viewpoint compresses space and draws attention to
    the land as pattern and surface rather than simply background.
  awnsers:
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 06e6f2e7b3b7bfb49a0d4ba2388cc4a5, type: 3}
